---
import SiteLayout from '@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/shared/PageHero';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Power Surfacing Render Worker | Batch Rendering | nPower Software"
  description="Render images and animations in batch mode on this computer or another Windows computer. Free Render Worker for Power Surfacing Viz, Studio, and RE Studio."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Power Surfacing Render Worker"
    subtitle="Render images and animations in batch mode on this computer or a different one."
    breadcrumbs={[
      { label: 'Product Downloads', path: '/pricing/downloads/#render-worker' },
      { label: 'Render Worker' },
    ]}
  />
  <section class="py-14 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
        <div class="lg:col-span-2 space-y-8">
          <section aria-labelledby="how-it-works">
            <h2 id="how-it-works" class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Batch rendering for your Power Surfacing projects</h2>
            <p class="text-slate-600 mb-3">A free companion product for Power Surfacing Viz, Studio, and RE Studio. Queue still images, turntables, and animations, then let the Render Worker process the jobs.</p>
            <p class="text-slate-600 mb-3">Run it on the same Windows computer as Power Surfacing, or on a different Windows computer to keep rendering work off your main machine.</p>
            <p class="text-slate-600">Prepare your scene and rendering settings in your Power Surfacing application, then send the job through a queue folder. The worker processes queued jobs and saves the rendered results for your application to collect. Cycles and LuxCore rendering engines and their required runtimes are included.</p>
          </section>
          <section aria-labelledby="getting-started">
            <h2 id="getting-started" class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Getting started</h2>
            <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-3 text-slate-600">
              <li>Run the installer on the Windows computer that will render your jobs and follow its setup instructions.</li>
              <li>Select a queue folder. For rendering on the same computer, use a local folder. For another computer, use a shared folder that both computers can read and write.</li>
              <li>Start the worker, then select that same queue folder in Power Surfacing's remote rendering settings.</li>
              <li>Prepare your scene and render settings in Power Surfacing, submit the jobs, and let the worker process the queue.</li>
            </ol>
          </section>
          <section aria-labelledby="gpu-rendering">
            <h2 id="gpu-rendering" class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">GPU rendering</h2>
            <p class="text-slate-600">For high performance GPU rendering of large assemblies, we recommend a graphics card with at least 8 GB of GPU memory.</p>
          </section>
          <section aria-labelledby="updating-worker">
            <h2 id="updating-worker" class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Updating an existing worker</h2>
            <p class="text-slate-600">Stop the worker after its current frames finish, close its control window, and run the new installer.</p>
          </section>
        </div>
        <aside class="self-start rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6" aria-label="Render Worker download">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Free Windows download</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4">No registration or license key is required for the Render Worker. A Power Surfacing application is needed to submit render jobs.</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-5">Windows x64 · Version 1.0.2026.1017<br />516 MiB · Released October 17, 2026<br />Signed by nPower Software</p>
          <a href="/Downloads/PowerSurfacing-RenderWorker-Setup-20261017.exe" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white bg-red-600 hover:bg-red-700 rounded-lg">Download Render Worker for Windows</a>
          <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-slate-500"><a href="/downloads/render-worker-20261017.sha256" class="underline hover:text-slate-700">SHA-256 checksum</a></p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-10"><a href="/pricing/downloads/#render-worker" class="text-sm font-semibold text-red-600 hover:text-red-700">Back to all Power Surfacing Studio downloads</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
